Building the trigger collection... I'm noticing the death-watch section is missing that same `if !desc.is_empty()` guard that protects the ETB-watch section, so it's creating triggers for every permanent regardless of whether they actually have death-watch abilities defined. Looking at the implementation, the `on_any_creature_dies` method fires whenever any creature dies while the Occultist is on the battlefield, triggering the mill choice. Since the `DeathWatch` trigger explicitly excludes the dead creature itself from its watcher list, and the `SelfDies` trigger handles the Occultist's own death separately, there's no double-triggering happening here.

But there's a critical issue with simultaneous deaths: when the Occultist dies in a board wipe alongside other creatures, the death-watch scan occurs after all creatures have moved to the graveyard, so the Occultist is no longer on the battlefield to trigger its `AnyCreatureDies` effect for the other dying creatures. This means you'd only get one mill from the Occultist's own `SelfDies` trigger instead of milling for each creature that died in the batch.

